## Object polymorphic holder ##
We use an Object polymorphic holder when a variable, method, or collection needs to handle different,
unrelated data types at the same time.
examples are : 
------------------------------------------------------
// Legacy ArrayList used Object arrays internally
ArrayList list = new ArrayList(); 
list.add("Hello");     // String treated as Object
list.add(2026);        // Integer treated as Object

// You must explicitly cast it back to use it
String str = (String) list.get(0); 
--------------------------------------------------------
// A row in a database table or Excel sheet
Object[] databaseRow = new Object[3];
databaseRow[0] = 101;                // ID (Integer)
databaseRow[1] = "Alice Smith";      // Name (String)
databaseRow[2] = true;               // Active status (Boolean)
----------------------------------------------------------
Creating Highly Flexible Methods
public void printLog(Object message) {
    // Accepts strings, dates, numbers, or custom objects
    System.out.println("LOG [" + System.currentTimeMillis() + "]: " + message.toString());
}
